    stem: "A 38-year-old woman asks about bowel cancer screening because 'cancer runs in the family'. You take a three-generation pedigree. Her mother had colorectal cancer at 44 and endometrial cancer at 49. Her maternal uncle had colorectal cancer at 51. Her maternal grandmother had a cancer of the 'waterworks' described as ureteric, in her fifties. The woman herself is asymptomatic with no personal history of bowel disease. Which single feature of this history should most change your management?",
