      C: 'Being asymptomatic is expected in a surveillance population and does not reduce the need for genetic assessment - surveillance exists precisely to detect disease before symptoms.',
      D: 'Population screening eligibility is irrelevant to someone at high familial risk; such patients need an individualised colonoscopic surveillance program, not faecal occult blood testing.',
