    stem: "A 31-year-old woman and her 33-year-old partner attend for preconception counselling. They plan to start trying for a pregnancy in the next few months. Neither has a personal or family history of genetic conditions and both are of northern European ancestry. They have read online about 'genetic carrier screening' and ask whether it is relevant to them, given that nobody in either family has anything wrong. What is the single most important point to convey and act on?",
